{"series":{"id":"wellbeing::selected-ssri-fills","label":"Six selected SSRIs · share of reported Medicare Part D 30-day fills","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"percent of reported standardized 30-day fills","scope":"us_states","definition":"","denominator":"","reporting_period":"2024","source_url":"https://data.cms.gov/provider-summary-by-type-of-service/medicare-part-d-prescribers/medicare-part-d-prescribers-by-geography-and-drug","sources":[{"id":"cms","title":"CMS Medicare Part D geography and drug data","url":"https://data.cms.gov/provider-summary-by-type-of-service/medicare-part-d-prescribers/medicare-part-d-prescribers-by-geography-and-drug","date":"2024","note":"Medicare Part D prescription claims; prescribing geography is not patient residence."}],"limitations":["These measures describe different questions, populations and time windows. They are not one happiness score.","Life satisfaction is a participating-state optional BRFSS module: missing states did not supply a comparable estimate here. Its curated table does not specify age adjustment.","The depression layer is directly published crude adult BRFSS lifetime diagnosis prevalence, not current symptoms, county averaging or age adjustment.","The past-year major-depressive-episode layer is a separate pooled 2023–2024 NSDUH small-area modeled estimate. Its intervals are Bayesian credible intervals, not the BRFSS survey confidence intervals.","A person can report past depression diagnosis and current life satisfaction. Care access affects whether illness is diagnosed.","The medicine layer covers six selected SSRI ingredients, not every antidepressant. It measures reported Medicare Part D fills by prescriber location, not patient residence or people taking medication.","Drug groups below 11 claims are suppressed. Medicines can have other indications; prescriptions do not establish depression or unhappiness.","Showing these maps next to resource maps does not establish that an industry, resource, or medicat